# Use-cases and workflows

- **Use-case**: one injectable, one verb, `execute(input, db?)` (or `execute(db?)` when there is no input), **full Drizzle SQL inline**. Size ≈ one repository method. No unrelated side effects.
- Optional positional `db?: DrizzleClient` — caller-owned tx or omit to use module db via `this.drizzle.client(db)`.
- **Workflow**: injectable orchestration — sequences use-cases + promote/thumbs/PIN hash/pubsub.
- Workflows that compose multiple DB steps open **one** `this.drizzle.db.transaction`, pass `tx` into every use-case inside, and run queue/pubsub **after commit**.
- Resolvers and tus hooks call **workflows** (or a single use-case when truly one verb).
- Do not collapse use-cases into static DB helper classes.
